.SP p2
.L 47.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]As the local police captain, Jiro keeps the force
.L 57.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]running, and the strain shows: he's jumpy, irritable,
.L 67.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]and always juggling several unrelated jobs at once,
.L 77.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]sometimes answering phones, barking orders, and
.L 87.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]doing paperwork all at the same time. His
.L 97.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]colleagues keep urging him to take time off, but
.L 107.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]he's never missed a day, and some suspect he's
.L 117.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]been saving up vacation for decades. Whether from
.L 127.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]stress or something darker, he tends to aim his
.L 137.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]gun at anything he considers an unwanted
.L 147.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]intrusion.
.CP
.SH
\&Jiro: Attacks
.PP
\&Desk-Side Revolver: Jiro's constant companion and likely only friend.
.PP
\&Bare Knuckle: While he prefers "civilized" weaponry like his revolver, Jiro can throw a mean punch.
.SH
\&Jiro: Character Hooks
.PP
\&For all his near-psychotic devotion to the job, Captain Jiro generally does it well. Still, even well-behaved PCs can find themselves under police scrutiny.
